# M6's done-when, first part: 1,000 ping-pong round trips between the root
# task and a server thread, timed with the TSC (user/root/src/pingpong.rs).
# The kernel has no test of this name, so the root task runs it. It
# retypes an endpoint and a TCB for the server S, at priority 200 with an
# IPC buffer in the second KiB of the root task's buffer frame, and calls
# S through a capability with badge 0x9090; S waits with Recv, then
# answers every request with ReplyRecv, checking the badge each time.
# Each run is 16 warm-up round trips, then 1,000 with an rdtsc between
# each two, every reply checked: the label's counter and MR0 come back
# plus one. In the full-length run MR4 to MR119 travel through both IPC
# buffers: S checks every word of each request and answers each plus one,
# and the root task checks every word of each reply. One-word messages
# first, the done-when's, then zero-length and 120-word ones; the root
# task prints how many round trips it checked, the total cycles of the
# timed ones and, per round trip, the mean, the fastest and the median,
# with nanoseconds from BootInfo's tsc_hz. Under TCG the numbers show
# trends, not performance, and the TSC follows host time: a busy host
# inflates the mean most.
cmdline: test=pingpong
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: cmdline: "test=pingpong"
expect: root: microL4 root task
expect: root: cmdline "test=pingpong"
expect: pingpong: server S (TCB slot
expect: priority 200, IPC buffer at
expect: badge 0x9090
expect: pingpong: 1016 round trips of 1-word messages, every reply checked, the last 1000 timed:
expect: TSC cycles in all; per round trip
expect: pingpong: 1016 round trips of 0-word messages, every reply checked, the last 1000 timed:
expect: TSC cycles in all; per round trip
expect: pingpong: 1016 round trips of 120-word messages, every reply checked, the last 1000 timed:
expect: TSC cycles in all; per round trip
expect: pingpong: nanoseconds at BootInfo's TSC rate
expect: pingpong: every full-length round trip carried MR4 to MR119 both ways: S checked each word it received and answered it plus one, and the root task checked each word of the reply
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
